1
00:01:24,084 --> 00:01:26,451
Ah, Jessie.

2
00:01:26,620 --> 00:01:28,521
Hi, Ben.

3
00:01:28,689 --> 00:01:31,591
So I guess Mom still thinks
you can talk me into anything.

4
00:01:31,758 --> 00:01:34,592
Well, she said since I talked
you into going to art school,

5
00:01:34,761 --> 00:01:36,753
maybe I can talk you
into going to school here.

6
00:01:37,464 --> 00:01:38,989
I'm going to L.A., Ben.

7
00:01:39,166 --> 00:01:40,464
Be reasonable, Jessie.

8
00:01:41,535 --> 00:01:43,834
She'll give you anything
you want if you stay here.

9
00:01:44,004 --> 00:01:46,974
But if you leave, she'll cut
you off without a thin dime.

10
00:01:47,140 --> 00:01:48,699
I know.

11
00:01:48,875 --> 00:01:50,673
Thanks, Ben, but I
wanna be on my own.

12
00:01:50,844 --> 00:01:52,779
It'll be good for me.

13
00:01:52,946 --> 00:01:57,782
Well, do...? Do you
have any money at all?

14
00:01:57,951 --> 00:02:01,888
I have my tuition and I sent out
a first month's rent to a girlfriend

15
00:02:02,055 --> 00:02:03,956
who's gonna be my roommate.

16
00:02:04,124 --> 00:02:06,593
- You won't change your mind?
- Nope.

17
00:02:06,760 --> 00:02:09,423
Well, take this.

18
00:02:09,596 --> 00:02:13,033
If you run into trouble, it's your
father's address and phone number.

19
00:02:15,235 --> 00:02:17,397
He's nobody's father.

20
00:02:18,505 --> 00:02:21,441
My daughter is as
stubborn as you are.

21
00:02:21,608 --> 00:02:23,406
- Attagirl.
- Heh.

22
00:02:23,577 --> 00:02:26,240
- Bye.
- Good luck.

23
00:04:10,984 --> 00:04:13,078
Beat it, pal.

24
00:04:58,565 --> 00:04:59,658
You're a girl.

25
00:05:03,603 --> 00:05:06,095
Yeah, and your place is a wreck.

26
00:05:06,907 --> 00:05:09,570
I don't remember
inviting you in.

27
00:05:11,178 --> 00:05:12,646
So tell me, do you
live with someone,

28
00:05:12,813 --> 00:05:15,305
or did you turn this place
into a slum all by yourself?

29
00:05:15,482 --> 00:05:19,442
Well, let's start with who are
you, and what do you want?

30
00:05:21,621 --> 00:05:23,954
I wanna be somewhere else.

31
00:05:27,027 --> 00:05:28,325
I'm your daughter, Max.

32
00:05:30,063 --> 00:05:31,361
You got any ID?

33
00:05:46,313 --> 00:05:47,975
You're Jessie.

34
00:05:49,449 --> 00:05:54,387
Well, you certainly grew up.

35
00:05:56,656 --> 00:05:58,284
What brings you to L.A.?

36
00:05:58,458 --> 00:06:00,586
Well, I don't wanna
put you out or anything,

37
00:06:00,760 --> 00:06:04,322
but my roommate
took off with my rent.

38
00:06:04,497 --> 00:06:08,559
It's a long story. I need a place to stay
for a couple of nights until I get a job.

39
00:06:08,735 --> 00:06:12,172
- Stay? Here?
- Is this asking too much?

40
00:06:12,339 --> 00:06:14,604
What about that guy your
mother married? He's loaded.

41
00:06:14,774 --> 00:06:16,834
Have him wire you some dough.

42
00:06:17,010 --> 00:06:19,411
No, no, no, see, we don't talk.

43
00:06:19,579 --> 00:06:21,172
He does what Mom wants

44
00:06:21,348 --> 00:06:24,045
and Mom wants me doing
her country club number.

45
00:06:24,217 --> 00:06:27,312
So do it. What do you
got against being rich?

46
00:06:30,790 --> 00:06:34,022
Apparently, this was a
mistake. I shouldn't have come.

47
00:06:34,194 --> 00:06:36,686
Oh, wait a minute. Now,
you can't wander around town.

48
00:06:36,863 --> 00:06:39,628
- I've got an extra bedroom.
- Just for a couple of nights.

49
00:06:39,799 --> 00:06:42,234
- Sure, until you get a job.
- Until I get a job.

50
00:07:09,996 --> 00:07:11,828
Do you mind if I
have some coffee?

51
00:07:11,998 --> 00:07:16,163
Help yourself. Donuts
are in the refrigerator.

52
00:07:21,341 --> 00:07:25,836
- Oh, wow, something die in here?
- Wanna clean it out?

53
00:07:26,012 --> 00:07:27,275
Wanna guess again?

54
00:07:34,988 --> 00:07:36,957
I'll get it.

55
00:07:43,096 --> 00:07:47,363
- Max. Hello, Max.
- Hi, Oscar.

56
00:07:47,534 --> 00:07:49,969
Well, how are we doing?

57
00:07:50,136 --> 00:07:53,072
- Got anything on Arlene yet?
- Not yet.

58
00:07:53,239 --> 00:07:57,438
But one of my operatives is gonna
stake that house out all day today.

59
00:07:57,610 --> 00:08:01,479
Wait, I thought you were gonna
handle my case personally.

60
00:08:01,648 --> 00:08:05,585
Oscar, it's not good procedure
for me to be seen too much.

61
00:08:05,752 --> 00:08:08,916
I mean, the neighbors get
excited, they call the cops.

62
00:08:09,089 --> 00:08:12,025
If Arlene spots me, she
could tip the boyfriend off.

63
00:08:12,192 --> 00:08:15,185
You're right. I wasn't thinking.
I'm not thinking right. My mind...

64
00:08:15,362 --> 00:08:17,092
That's what you pay me for.

65
00:08:17,263 --> 00:08:20,165
By the way, that operative I
mentioned to you, today's payday.

66
00:08:20,333 --> 00:08:22,666
- Five hundred bucks.
- This is getting expensive.

67
00:08:22,836 --> 00:08:24,031
The best costs.

68
00:08:25,405 --> 00:08:28,500
"Justice is neither
swift nor cheap."

69
00:08:28,675 --> 00:08:32,168
- Oliver Wendell Holmes.
- Ugh, you're telling me.

70
00:08:32,645 --> 00:08:36,173
Five hundred. Listen, the
boyfriend, what's he like?

71
00:08:36,349 --> 00:08:39,012
Young? Have a lot of hair?

72
00:08:39,185 --> 00:08:41,848
I don't know. I
haven't seen him yet.

73
00:08:42,022 --> 00:08:44,753
- Good luck.
- Yeah, you too, Oscar.

74
00:08:48,695 --> 00:08:50,630
Oliver Wendell Holmes?

75
00:08:51,898 --> 00:08:55,562
- Mary Holmes?
- How many operatives do you have?

76
00:08:55,735 --> 00:08:59,433
As of today, just you.

77
00:08:59,606 --> 00:09:01,939
I am not a detective, Max.

78
00:09:02,108 --> 00:09:05,272
It's either that or clean
out the refrigerator.

79
00:09:06,946 --> 00:09:09,074
- Go to this address.
- Okay.

80
00:09:09,249 --> 00:09:11,309
Here's a map.

81
00:09:11,484 --> 00:09:13,976
Take a picture of everybody
that goes in and out of there.

82
00:09:14,154 --> 00:09:15,178
Why?

83
00:09:15,355 --> 00:09:18,348
Oscar's still paying his
ex-wife Arlene alimony.

84
00:09:18,525 --> 00:09:20,824
Some other guy's keeping her.

85
00:09:21,394 --> 00:09:23,954
We prove that,
Oscar's off the hook.

86
00:09:24,130 --> 00:09:27,100
Are you sure Oscar
isn't just being vindictive?

87
00:09:27,267 --> 00:09:30,260
Truth is, he's still
hung up on her.

88
00:09:30,437 --> 00:09:33,839
- I didn't hear him say that.
- I don't have to.

89
00:09:34,007 --> 00:09:35,236
I'll see you later.

90
00:09:35,408 --> 00:09:37,639
I've got an important
meeting in Arcadia.

91
00:09:37,811 --> 00:09:39,245
Okay.

92
00:09:39,412 --> 00:09:40,903
Is that a TV antenna?

93
00:09:41,081 --> 00:09:44,313
This is the sculpture that got
me into the L.A. Art Institute.

94
00:09:44,484 --> 00:09:46,009
It's called Tangled Web.

95
00:09:46,619 --> 00:09:50,078
Oh. Beautiful.

96
00:10:26,626 --> 00:10:29,118
Hold it right there.

97
00:10:32,098 --> 00:10:33,122
Kitty, kitty, kitty.

98
00:10:34,467 --> 00:10:37,767
Heh. Hi, kitty

99
00:12:34,120 --> 00:12:37,113
<i>Thanks, Ann. At shortly
after 3 this afternoon,</i>

100
00:12:37,290 --> 00:12:39,691
<i>Ms. Arlene Treadwell was
found strangled to death</i>

101
00:12:39,859 --> 00:12:41,191
<i>at her home in Westwood.</i>

102
00:12:41,361 --> 00:12:43,161
<i>Police were summoned
to the scene by neighbors</i>

103
00:12:43,296 --> 00:12:46,266
<i>when they heard a car careening
off a parked vehicle. Police...</i>

104
00:12:46,432 --> 00:12:47,991
What's this?

105
00:12:48,167 --> 00:12:51,331
I guess Oscar's ex won't be
cashing any more of his checks.

106
00:12:51,504 --> 00:12:56,306
And like they say in the movies,
I've got the goods on the killer.

107
00:12:56,476 --> 00:12:58,638
Nice work, Jessie.

108
00:13:00,813 --> 00:13:02,145
Social call, fellas?

109
00:13:02,315 --> 00:13:05,080
Just dropped by to remind
you that today's payday.

110
00:13:05,251 --> 00:13:08,483
- Tell Tony tomorrow.
- Hey.

111
00:13:08,655 --> 00:13:12,319
Had it today, but you
blew it at the track, right?

112
00:13:15,328 --> 00:13:19,095
You don't wanna hang out with
him, honey, he's got no future.

113
00:13:24,470 --> 00:13:27,235
- You're in trouble, aren't you?
- A little.

114
00:13:28,875 --> 00:13:31,003
You owe some guy
named Tony a lot of money

115
00:13:31,177 --> 00:13:34,375
and you used the $500 from
Oscar to try to win it at the track?

116
00:13:35,014 --> 00:13:36,880
Yeah, I know.

117
00:13:37,417 --> 00:13:38,977
Who would have
thought it wouldn't work?

118
00:13:52,165 --> 00:13:56,500
Well, thanks to you,
we've got our suspect.

119
00:13:56,669 --> 00:13:58,069
He's on his way down.

120
00:13:58,237 --> 00:14:00,968
You are turning into
a model citizen, Max.

121
00:14:01,140 --> 00:14:02,580
I'd like to claim
all of the credit,

122
00:14:02,742 --> 00:14:04,677
but my offspring
here took the pictures.

123
00:14:04,844 --> 00:14:07,609
You're...? You're his daughter?
- Mm-hm.

124
00:14:07,780 --> 00:14:10,181
- Jessie Morgan.
- Alison Darnell.

125
00:14:10,350 --> 00:14:12,819
Daddy, what big
surprises you have.

126
00:14:12,985 --> 00:14:14,647
Hmm, I'm a parent.

127
00:14:14,821 --> 00:14:18,451
I'm a taxpayer, I work hard,
I'm a responsible citizen.

128
00:14:18,624 --> 00:14:22,493
- Was he always this noble?
- I wouldn't know.

129
00:14:22,662 --> 00:14:24,426
Of course, now that
the case is closed,

130
00:14:24,597 --> 00:14:26,862
I'm also here because
my client can pay me.

131
00:14:27,033 --> 00:14:30,936
Wait. Wait a minute. This
is a mistake. I didn't do it.

132
00:14:31,104 --> 00:14:33,096
- Oscar.
- Max. Max, you gotta help me.

133
00:14:33,272 --> 00:14:35,537
This is a mistake,
a terrible mistake.

134
00:14:35,708 --> 00:14:38,109
- Max!
- What is he doing here?

135
00:14:38,277 --> 00:14:40,678
We just arrested him
for the murder of his wife

136
00:14:40,847 --> 00:14:43,681
and your evidence
is gonna nail him.

137
00:14:53,426 --> 00:14:54,860
Poor Arlene.

138
00:14:55,027 --> 00:14:59,965
This is terrible. Just awful.
- I'm really sorry.

139
00:15:00,666 --> 00:15:03,067
You gave them pictures of
my car. How could you do that?

140
00:15:03,236 --> 00:15:05,933
- I'm sorry, I didn't know.
- Sorry?

141
00:15:06,105 --> 00:15:08,336
I've been framed for murder.
You helped them do it.

142
00:15:08,508 --> 00:15:10,477
- Oscar.
- I feel dizzy.

143
00:15:10,643 --> 00:15:13,078
Look, the kid didn't
know about the car.

144
00:15:13,246 --> 00:15:15,511
Neither did I.
Let's get past that.

145
00:15:16,182 --> 00:15:21,780
The really bad news is, the rope
that was used to strangle Arlene

146
00:15:21,954 --> 00:15:24,423
was found in your trash.

147
00:15:24,824 --> 00:15:29,057
And the damage to your car
matches the car on the scene.

148
00:15:29,962 --> 00:15:31,453
Now, do you have an alibi?

149
00:15:31,631 --> 00:15:33,600
Alibi? No, I...

150
00:15:33,766 --> 00:15:38,363
I got a call to go meet Arlene
on a street corner near my office

151
00:15:38,538 --> 00:15:40,905
and the guy that called
said he was her lawyer

152
00:15:41,073 --> 00:15:42,371
and she wanted to negotiate.

153
00:15:42,542 --> 00:15:45,603
So I went. I waited about
an hour. She never showed.

154
00:15:45,778 --> 00:15:49,874
- Did anybody see you there?
- It's a side street, practically deserted.

155
00:15:50,049 --> 00:15:51,210
Oh, what am I gonna do?

156
00:15:51,384 --> 00:15:54,183
- Did Arlene have a key to your car?
- Yes.

157
00:15:54,353 --> 00:15:55,480
She never returned it.

158
00:15:56,789 --> 00:16:01,056
That means the anonymous
boyfriend has access to your car.

159
00:16:01,594 --> 00:16:05,929
Max, I wanna hire you
to prove I didn't do it.

160
00:16:06,098 --> 00:16:08,897
Oscar, you already hired me.
You don't have to hire me again.

161
00:16:09,068 --> 00:16:10,627
I'm still working for you.

162
00:16:10,803 --> 00:16:13,363
And, listen, I'm sorry if I
went after you like that.

163
00:16:13,539 --> 00:16:15,269
Oh, no, no, no, that's
okay. You're upset.

164
00:16:15,441 --> 00:16:18,809
- You've had a bad day.
- Yeah. Oh, it's...

165
00:16:18,978 --> 00:16:21,504
Oh, poor Arlene.

166
00:16:21,681 --> 00:16:23,582
She was so confused.

167
00:16:23,749 --> 00:16:26,742
I didn't care about
the money, not really.

168
00:16:27,420 --> 00:16:29,321
It's just I didn't
wanna lose her.

169
00:16:32,692 --> 00:16:34,820
I really loved her.

170
00:16:39,699 --> 00:16:41,930
I feel terrible, Max.
This is all my fault.

171
00:16:42,101 --> 00:16:43,592
No, you just did
what I told you.

172
00:16:43,769 --> 00:16:45,809
Well, you're going to help
the poor guy, aren't you?

173
00:16:45,938 --> 00:16:49,431
If I don't, I'll never
get the rest of my fee.

174
00:16:49,609 --> 00:16:51,635
Nobody is that cynical.

175
00:16:51,811 --> 00:16:53,302
No, I'm not.

176
00:16:53,479 --> 00:16:58,281
But I owe Tony Myers 10,000
bucks, and he is very cynical.

177
00:17:10,897 --> 00:17:13,799
Ah, just like home.

178
00:17:19,405 --> 00:17:22,603
Phone's dead. Maybe
somebody forgot to pay the bills.

179
00:17:22,775 --> 00:17:24,903
You sound like your mother.

180
00:17:25,077 --> 00:17:26,807
So tell me about it, Max.

181
00:17:26,979 --> 00:17:30,040
Seems you used to be some
big deal Hollywood detective.

182
00:17:30,216 --> 00:17:32,310
- What happened?
- Well, the women got faster

183
00:17:32,485 --> 00:17:34,420
and the horses got slower.

184
00:17:34,587 --> 00:17:36,453
- How's your mother?
- Perfect.

185
00:17:36,622 --> 00:17:39,888
I remember. What's
her new husband like?

186
00:17:40,059 --> 00:17:41,083
Obedient.

187
00:17:41,260 --> 00:17:42,853
Aha.

188
00:17:43,329 --> 00:17:47,357
Did you ever graduate from that
fancy women's college back east?

189
00:17:47,533 --> 00:17:49,126
How'd you know I went there?

190
00:17:50,002 --> 00:17:52,801
Read about it in
<i>Newsweek.</i> What happened?

191
00:17:53,739 --> 00:17:54,798
I got bored.

192
00:17:56,709 --> 00:17:58,371
What happened?

193
00:17:59,645 --> 00:18:01,045
I got bounced.

194
00:18:01,213 --> 00:18:03,341
Hmm, you're a tough
case, aren't you?

195
00:18:03,516 --> 00:18:07,351
What makes you think you're
gonna do any better in art school?

196
00:18:07,520 --> 00:18:10,183
Well, um, I like doing
things with my hands.

197
00:18:10,356 --> 00:18:12,222
You know, sculpture
and water colors.

198
00:18:12,391 --> 00:18:15,589
I like to make art out of
junk that people throw away.

199
00:18:15,761 --> 00:18:17,195
And I'm good too.

200
00:18:17,363 --> 00:18:20,492
- I don't know where I get it.
- My mother was an artist.

201
00:18:20,666 --> 00:18:23,363
She made her living
drawing greeting cards.

202
00:18:23,536 --> 00:18:25,061
She wanted to paint.

203
00:18:25,237 --> 00:18:27,763
But it's hard to be a
starving artist and raise a kid.

204
00:18:27,940 --> 00:18:29,568
She was good.

205
00:18:29,909 --> 00:18:31,109
Maybe that's where you got it.

206
00:18:31,811 --> 00:18:33,507
Maybe.

207
00:18:43,923 --> 00:18:46,324
So, Max, tell me again
what we're doing here.

208
00:18:46,492 --> 00:18:49,087
I'm gonna check out Oscar's car.

209
00:18:57,803 --> 00:19:01,433
- What are you looking for?
- The last number called.

210
00:19:02,141 --> 00:19:04,007
Let's give them a ring.

211
00:19:08,681 --> 00:19:10,201
WOMAN: <i>Starling residence.</i>

212
00:19:10,349 --> 00:19:12,909
Hello, is Herman
Starling there, please?

213
00:19:13,085 --> 00:19:14,109
<i>Uh, no, sir.</i>

214
00:19:14,286 --> 00:19:16,687
<i>This is the residence of
Mr. and Mrs. Jack Starling.</i>

215
00:19:16,856 --> 00:19:19,792
<i>- You've got the wrong number.</i>
- Oh.

216
00:19:19,959 --> 00:19:21,825
Thank you very much.

217
00:19:24,296 --> 00:19:26,128
We might have something big.

218
00:19:26,966 --> 00:19:29,197
- What do you mean, big?
- That's Jack Starling's house.

219
00:19:29,368 --> 00:19:32,236
Starling's a film director.

220
00:19:32,405 --> 00:19:36,866
He's been in and out. He directs
films with numbers after them

221
00:19:37,043 --> 00:19:40,980
like <i>Death Watch
6</i> and <i>Obliterator 7.</i>

222
00:19:41,147 --> 00:19:43,187
He married an heiress and
she's putting up the money

223
00:19:43,315 --> 00:19:46,114
- for his first A picture.
- So, what now?

224
00:19:46,285 --> 00:19:48,811
Well, somebody
called Starling's house.

225
00:19:48,988 --> 00:19:52,584
If Oscar didn't do it,
maybe our killer did.

226
00:19:53,359 --> 00:19:55,021
Arlene kept a pretty neat house.

227
00:20:02,768 --> 00:20:06,068
No sign of the boyfriend, not
even a beer in the refrigerator.

228
00:20:06,238 --> 00:20:09,333
- Maybe he's married.
- Why do you say that?

229
00:20:09,508 --> 00:20:10,703
Well, when he killed her,

230
00:20:10,876 --> 00:20:13,471
he wasn't in here long
enough to clean the place out

231
00:20:13,646 --> 00:20:15,945
and married men are very
careful in these situations.

232
00:20:16,582 --> 00:20:18,175
Are they?

233
00:20:26,859 --> 00:20:29,761
- Hey, look at this.
- Cuff link.

234
00:20:29,929 --> 00:20:31,420
Expensive.

235
00:20:31,597 --> 00:20:34,328
Look. "For my J."

236
00:20:34,500 --> 00:20:37,129
May 22nd, 1988.

237
00:20:37,303 --> 00:20:39,829
J, as in Mr. Big-Movie-Guy,
Jack Starling.

238
00:20:40,005 --> 00:20:41,906
Could be.

239
00:20:42,575 --> 00:20:45,477
Maybe Arlene was pressing
him for a commitment,

240
00:20:45,644 --> 00:20:46,804
threatening to tell his wife.

241
00:20:46,946 --> 00:20:48,972
So he killed her. Nice guy.

242
00:20:49,749 --> 00:20:52,150
If he did, he's
got a big problem.

243
00:20:52,318 --> 00:20:55,083
His wife probably
gave him these cufflinks.

244
00:20:55,254 --> 00:20:57,246
That means he's got
to get this one back.

245
00:21:10,536 --> 00:21:13,096
- Party time.
- Looks like it.

246
00:21:13,706 --> 00:21:17,040
But how am I gonna get in
there without getting caught?

247
00:21:17,209 --> 00:21:18,973
Pretend we're florists.

248
00:21:19,145 --> 00:21:21,842
- I don't look like a florist.
- I do.

249
00:21:22,014 --> 00:21:23,482
No.

250
00:21:25,017 --> 00:21:27,316
No, you don't.

251
00:22:25,077 --> 00:22:26,511
Something I can do for you?

252
00:22:47,299 --> 00:22:48,927
I got caught.

253
00:22:49,101 --> 00:22:51,263
- Swell.
- Very swell.

254
00:22:51,437 --> 00:22:53,633
We got invited to the party.

255
00:23:01,447 --> 00:23:03,047
So anyway, I was
rifling through the desk

256
00:23:03,215 --> 00:23:04,535
and I heard this
noise behind me,

257
00:23:04,683 --> 00:23:07,346
and I whirled around and
there is the oh-so glamorous

258
00:23:07,519 --> 00:23:10,250
but very annoyed Mrs.
Jack Starling herself.

259
00:23:10,422 --> 00:23:13,586
Now, I know from experience that
the best defense is a good offense.

260
00:23:13,759 --> 00:23:17,196
So I got right in her face and
I said, "That is a great dress.

261
00:23:17,363 --> 00:23:18,490
Where did you get it?"

262
00:23:18,664 --> 00:23:20,544
Of course, she's too
flattered to not answer me.

263
00:23:20,699 --> 00:23:22,019
So while she's
like "Blah, blah."

264
00:23:22,167 --> 00:23:24,227
I realized that I just
saw a picture of her

265
00:23:24,403 --> 00:23:26,065
at a Bryn Mawr
reunion on her desk.

266
00:23:26,238 --> 00:23:28,469
So I tell her that I was
at Bryn Mawr myself,

267
00:23:28,641 --> 00:23:30,269
which I was, for almost
a whole semester,

268
00:23:30,442 --> 00:23:32,707
before I got bounced
for... Never mind.

269
00:23:32,878 --> 00:23:34,904
Anyway, we kind of hit it off.

270
00:23:35,080 --> 00:23:37,345
She's sort of like
Mom, you know?

271
00:23:37,516 --> 00:23:39,144
Vague.

272
00:23:40,386 --> 00:23:41,877
Max, hurry up.
We're gonna be late.

273
00:23:45,591 --> 00:23:47,355
Shall we dance?

274
00:24:01,507 --> 00:24:03,373
Jessie Morgan and guest.

275
00:24:03,542 --> 00:24:06,307
Ms. Morgan, sir,
Have a good time.

276
00:24:18,190 --> 00:24:22,321
To your left, wearing a simple frock
of spun gold and discreet emeralds,

277
00:24:22,494 --> 00:24:25,794
- Mrs. Jack Starling.
- On your right, short, dark

278
00:24:25,965 --> 00:24:27,729
and untalented Mr. Starling.

279
00:24:31,136 --> 00:24:33,016
Okay, I'm gonna see
if I can find the cuff link.

280
00:24:33,138 --> 00:24:34,778
Make sure Starling
doesn't leave the room.

281
00:24:34,907 --> 00:24:36,933
- Wait a minute.
- Mr. Starling.

282
00:24:37,109 --> 00:24:39,203
Hi, I'm Jessie Morgan.

283
00:24:39,378 --> 00:24:41,098
Nice to meet you. I'm
a friend of your wife.

284
00:24:41,246 --> 00:24:42,680
- Ah.
- I'd like you to meet my dad.

285
00:24:42,848 --> 00:24:44,612
- Ah.
- He's a huge fan of yours.

286
00:24:44,783 --> 00:24:46,718
I never miss one of
your movies, Jack.

287
00:24:46,885 --> 00:24:49,184
- Really?
- Yeah. <i>Death Raid 3.</i>

288
00:24:49,355 --> 00:24:52,723
That was my favorite,
yeah. How about a drink?

289
00:24:52,891 --> 00:24:53,915
- Really?
- Yeah.

290
00:24:54,093 --> 00:24:55,925
Oh, are you kidding?

291
00:26:48,373 --> 00:26:49,893
I heard you are
working on a movie

292
00:26:50,042 --> 00:26:51,533
of the Red Gardenia Murder Case.

293
00:26:51,710 --> 00:26:53,406
Yes, Mr. Morgan, we are.

294
00:26:53,579 --> 00:26:56,515
I knew Nick
Ballinger worked on it.

295
00:27:01,053 --> 00:27:02,544
I still am.

296
00:27:03,255 --> 00:27:06,316
Sorry we hadn't gotten to know each
other when you were prepping this.

297
00:27:06,492 --> 00:27:09,428
I know some inside
stuff that really happened.

298
00:27:11,330 --> 00:27:15,028
Um, I guess you
finished writing it by now.

299
00:27:15,200 --> 00:27:17,920
We're more than finished, Mr. Morgan.
We're halfway through shooting.

300
00:27:18,070 --> 00:27:21,871
Listen, I really must get back.
It's, uh... It's good to meet you.

301
00:27:22,040 --> 00:27:25,101
Actually, I'm working on
something that might interest you.

302
00:27:25,277 --> 00:27:26,905
Happened today.

303
00:27:27,079 --> 00:27:29,514
Woman got killed in
a condo in Westwood.

304
00:27:30,883 --> 00:27:33,717
Yeah, it was on the news, uh...

305
00:27:33,886 --> 00:27:35,912
Accountant murdered his ex-wife.

306
00:27:36,088 --> 00:27:37,989
Well, that's what
the cops think.

307
00:27:38,690 --> 00:27:43,253
Actually, I happen to know
she was killed by her boyfriend.

308
00:27:43,428 --> 00:27:48,264
- Really? How would you know that?
- I've got a key piece of evidence.

309
00:27:48,433 --> 00:27:51,870
The killer left a
cuff link behind.

310
00:27:52,037 --> 00:27:53,835
Would you believe it?

311
00:27:55,574 --> 00:27:57,167
It's getting late.

312
00:27:57,342 --> 00:28:01,302
I gotta find my
daughter, get her home.

313
00:28:02,714 --> 00:28:04,706
I'll call you in the morning.

314
00:28:05,450 --> 00:28:07,078
Fine.

315
00:28:07,252 --> 00:28:09,448
Pleasure to meet
you, Mr. Morgan.

316
00:28:09,621 --> 00:28:11,180
Good night.

317
00:28:16,061 --> 00:28:20,192
Darling, it's time to go home.

318
00:28:23,101 --> 00:28:24,729
Come on.

319
00:28:24,903 --> 00:28:29,170
- Unh! What took you so long?
- Let's go home.

320
00:28:30,576 --> 00:28:32,909
- You find anything?
- I didn't have a chance.

321
00:28:33,078 --> 00:28:35,638
Don't worry. You
gave it your best shot.

322
00:28:35,814 --> 00:28:39,251
Please don't take me off the case.
I'm the one who got Oscar in trouble.

323
00:28:39,418 --> 00:28:41,717
Look, Starling
could be dangerous.

324
00:28:41,887 --> 00:28:43,947
Only one of us needs
to get close to him.

325
00:28:44,122 --> 00:28:47,650
That's me. So I'm
in and you're out.

326
00:28:47,826 --> 00:28:50,057
You can't tell me what to do.

327
00:28:50,229 --> 00:28:54,064
- Go to art school.
- Classes don't start till next week.

328
00:28:54,233 --> 00:28:56,828
The trash is full of beer cans.
Make something creative.

329
00:28:59,004 --> 00:29:03,408
- Somebody's in your bedroom.
- I'll look into it.

330
00:29:04,509 --> 00:29:05,704
Hi. JESSIE: Alison?

331
00:29:05,877 --> 00:29:09,609
Jessie, jeez, you look gorgeous.

332
00:29:10,015 --> 00:29:13,713
And you, you're so late that
I decided to wash my hair.

333
00:29:17,089 --> 00:29:18,682
Mm.

334
00:29:19,958 --> 00:29:21,517
Good night.

335
00:29:30,335 --> 00:29:34,670
Well, it's, uh... It's important
to have friends on the force.

336
00:29:35,607 --> 00:29:37,132
Good night, Max.

337
00:29:42,047 --> 00:29:43,709
Come in.

338
00:29:45,350 --> 00:29:46,875
Do you need anything?

339
00:29:47,052 --> 00:29:48,680
Sheets? Towels?

340
00:29:48,854 --> 00:29:51,346
I got some fancy soap
some wise guy gave me

341
00:29:51,523 --> 00:29:52,889
at Christmas around
here somewhere.

342
00:29:53,058 --> 00:29:54,424
You're embarrassed.

343
00:29:56,795 --> 00:29:58,286
Why would I be embarrassed?

344
00:29:59,164 --> 00:30:00,655
You tell me.

345
00:30:01,900 --> 00:30:04,563
How come you know so
much about married men?

346
00:30:07,272 --> 00:30:09,298
You're the detective,
Max. You figure it out.

347
00:30:10,809 --> 00:30:13,870
You're right. None
of my business.

348
00:30:14,646 --> 00:30:17,946
- Good night.
- He was a philosophy professor.

349
00:30:21,820 --> 00:30:23,755
Very smart.

350
00:30:26,091 --> 00:30:27,889
Very married.

351
00:30:29,428 --> 00:30:30,953
Very sweet to me.

352
00:30:34,566 --> 00:30:36,057
So...

353
00:30:39,371 --> 00:30:41,203
You had a thing.

354
00:30:41,373 --> 00:30:43,604
Somebody found
out. You got bounced.

355
00:30:45,444 --> 00:30:46,810
What about him?

356
00:30:47,346 --> 00:30:51,147
Tenure. He was unbounceable.

357
00:30:51,316 --> 00:30:56,721
So I left school and
he didn't call me.

358
00:30:57,489 --> 00:31:00,186
Mom's shrink said it
was your fault, you know.

359
00:31:00,359 --> 00:31:02,157
"Growing up without
a dad" syndrome.

360
00:31:02,327 --> 00:31:05,525
Well, now, you know your
mother pays her shrink extra

361
00:31:05,697 --> 00:31:07,859
- to blow smoke like that.
- Heh.

362
00:31:11,737 --> 00:31:13,831
You deserve better.
You know that.

363
00:31:16,341 --> 00:31:17,900
I'm working on it.

364
00:31:22,180 --> 00:31:24,411
First one up makes coffee.

365
00:31:25,817 --> 00:31:27,012
Good night.

366
00:31:28,086 --> 00:31:29,520
Good night.

367
00:32:29,147 --> 00:32:32,208
<i>"Dear Jessie.
Happy third birthday.</i>

368
00:32:32,784 --> 00:32:35,754
<i>Since I can't be there,
I'm sending you Henry.</i>

369
00:32:35,921 --> 00:32:38,481
<i>He looks just like an
ordinary teddy bear,</i>

370
00:32:38,657 --> 00:32:40,250
<i>but he has a secret.</i>

371
00:32:40,425 --> 00:32:43,623
<i>In the middle of the night,
when you're sound asleep,</i>

372
00:32:43,795 --> 00:32:46,060
<i>he'll whisper messages from me.</i>

373
00:32:46,231 --> 00:32:50,066
<i>He'll tell you I'm thinking
of you and missing you</i>

374
00:32:50,235 --> 00:32:53,364
<i>and hoping to see
you very, very soon.</i>

375
00:32:53,538 --> 00:32:56,667
<i>Love you, baby. Always will.</i>

376
00:32:56,842 --> 00:33:00,870
<i>And someday, we'll
be together again.</i>

377
00:33:01,046 --> 00:33:04,016
<i>I love you. Daddy."</i>

378
00:33:39,651 --> 00:33:44,453
Yeah, Jack, I thought this
case might be right up your alley.

379
00:33:45,323 --> 00:33:47,519
Oh, yeah, I got the cuff link.

380
00:33:47,692 --> 00:33:51,288
Yeah, I do think it would be
a good idea if we got together.

381
00:33:51,463 --> 00:33:53,261
What about now?

382
00:33:53,932 --> 00:33:55,901
Where are you shooting?

383
00:33:57,269 --> 00:33:59,602
Well, where in Canyon Country?

384
00:34:00,472 --> 00:34:02,464
Yeah. Yeah.

385
00:34:02,641 --> 00:34:05,440
Oh, yeah, I can find it. Bye.

386
00:34:05,610 --> 00:34:07,909
- Morning.
- Morning.

387
00:34:08,947 --> 00:34:10,939
- What's up?
- That was Jack Starling.

388
00:34:11,116 --> 00:34:13,608
I got some inside information
on the Red Gardenia case

389
00:34:13,785 --> 00:34:15,344
he can use shooting his movie.

390
00:34:15,520 --> 00:34:17,751
- I'm gonna go see him.
- You want me to come with you?

391
00:34:17,923 --> 00:34:22,657
Oh, no, you just hang out, be
creative, paint the dining room.

392
00:35:12,611 --> 00:35:14,603
You wouldn't be kidding
me about this, would you?

393
00:35:14,779 --> 00:35:16,839
I never kid about serious money.

394
00:35:17,015 --> 00:35:20,452
Mr. Starling, the stunt's all set
up. We're ready when you are.

395
00:35:20,619 --> 00:35:24,386
Trevor, take your hand
off me, and yes, I am ready.

396
00:35:31,296 --> 00:35:34,323
If I was going to the cops,
you'd be in the slammer by now.

397
00:35:34,499 --> 00:35:36,297
But I got some bills to pay.

398
00:35:36,468 --> 00:35:39,700
- The cuff link's yours for 100 grand.
- Heh.

399
00:35:39,871 --> 00:35:42,500
- You're out of your mind.
- And you're out of luck.

400
00:35:42,674 --> 00:35:47,237
The engraving says, "To
my J, May 22nd, 1988."

401
00:35:47,412 --> 00:35:49,244
Take it or leave it.

402
00:35:51,650 --> 00:35:53,642
We finish this picture tonight.

403
00:35:53,818 --> 00:35:57,186
Stage 8. I'll bring the money,
you bring the cuff link, 9:00.

404
00:35:57,355 --> 00:35:59,256
Smart move, Jack.

405
00:35:59,424 --> 00:36:02,417
Charlie, baby, hear me good.

406
00:36:04,396 --> 00:36:06,331
Bradford.

407
00:36:06,498 --> 00:36:08,091
Bradford!

408
00:36:08,266 --> 00:36:11,896
Take the donut out of your
mouth and let's shoot this.

409
00:36:30,722 --> 00:36:33,385
Roll cameras. Action.

410
00:36:42,534 --> 00:36:44,264
Hey, wait!

411
00:36:55,313 --> 00:36:57,353
- All right, everybody happy with that?
- We got it.

412
00:36:57,482 --> 00:37:00,384
- Wrap it.
- That's a wrap, folks.

413
00:37:04,355 --> 00:37:07,484
- I'll see you tonight.
- Oh, yeah.

414
00:37:55,740 --> 00:37:58,039
Testing. Testing.

415
00:37:59,844 --> 00:38:01,938
<i>Testing. Testing.</i>

416
00:38:02,413 --> 00:38:04,245
Where do you think you're going?

417
00:38:04,415 --> 00:38:06,111
I heard you on the
set with Starling, Max.

418
00:38:06,284 --> 00:38:07,980
You're selling out for money.

419
00:38:08,953 --> 00:38:10,285
I had to tell him that.

420
00:38:10,455 --> 00:38:12,335
If I'm gonna nail him, I
gotta get close to him.

421
00:38:12,490 --> 00:38:14,891
- Well, then why did you lie to me?
- I told you.

422
00:38:15,059 --> 00:38:16,493
He's dangerous.

423
00:38:16,661 --> 00:38:19,426
I'm trying to keep you out of this,
but you won't do what I tell you.

424
00:38:20,465 --> 00:38:22,297
You know, I wish I
could believe you.

425
00:38:24,502 --> 00:38:25,697
Give me the cuff link.

426
00:38:25,870 --> 00:38:30,399
You know, I found all those cards and
letters and presents that you sent me

427
00:38:30,575 --> 00:38:34,205
that Mom apparently sent back,
and for one tiny moment I thought,

428
00:38:34,379 --> 00:38:35,847
"What do you know about that?

429
00:38:36,014 --> 00:38:38,813
Maybe he's not such
a bad guy after all."

430
00:38:39,350 --> 00:38:42,320
Well, you can keep
your teddy bear, Max.

431
00:38:42,487 --> 00:38:45,457
You're the bum Mom
always said you were.

432
00:38:45,623 --> 00:38:47,421
Anything for money.

433
00:39:06,377 --> 00:39:08,869
That dirty little
double-crosser.

434
00:39:58,062 --> 00:39:59,894
Starling.

435
00:40:03,568 --> 00:40:05,730
Jack Starling?

436
00:40:14,946 --> 00:40:16,244
Starling.

437
00:40:25,690 --> 00:40:26,714
Where's your father?

438
00:40:28,693 --> 00:40:31,390
He's working late at the
office. Do you have the money?

439
00:40:33,798 --> 00:40:34,891
What do you have for me?

440
00:40:39,304 --> 00:40:40,567
Show me the money first.

441
00:40:42,140 --> 00:40:44,735
"Show me the money
first." Heh. Why not?

442
00:40:46,544 --> 00:40:48,240
Why not?

443
00:40:51,215 --> 00:40:54,743
- Would you like to count it?
- Yes, I would.

444
00:41:03,695 --> 00:41:05,027
Pretty expensive cuff link.

445
00:41:05,196 --> 00:41:07,062
Hundred thousand dollars

446
00:41:07,231 --> 00:41:09,393
- just for one of them?
- Sentimental value.

447
00:41:09,567 --> 00:41:10,847
Next time you murder a mistress,

448
00:41:11,002 --> 00:41:12,682
it might cost you a
little more than money.

449
00:41:12,837 --> 00:41:15,272
I'll try not to make the
same mistake twice.

450
00:41:15,440 --> 00:41:17,602
Good. It'll be a lot easier
on the next girl that way.

451
00:41:17,775 --> 00:41:21,712
- So the money's all here.
- Here's your cuff link.

452
00:41:26,351 --> 00:41:27,410
Uh-huh.

453
00:41:27,585 --> 00:41:30,350
Now, if you'll give me
the wire you're wearing...

454
00:41:34,325 --> 00:41:36,157
- Wire?
- I believe that's a tape recorder

455
00:41:36,327 --> 00:41:37,351
in your pocket.

456
00:41:37,762 --> 00:41:40,288
- Oh, tape recorder. Right.
- Give me the...

457
00:41:49,140 --> 00:41:51,507
- You give it to me. MAX:
Put that gun down, Jack.

458
00:41:51,676 --> 00:41:53,110
Max!

459
00:41:56,814 --> 00:41:57,941
Give it up, Jack.

460
00:41:58,116 --> 00:42:00,585
You heard the man, Jack.
- Put it down.

461
00:42:02,887 --> 00:42:05,447
Arlene threatened to tell
your wife about the affair.

462
00:42:05,623 --> 00:42:07,216
Didn't she, Jack?

463
00:42:07,392 --> 00:42:08,587
You'd have lost your wife.

464
00:42:08,760 --> 00:42:11,559
No money, no movie,
end of Jack Starling.

465
00:42:11,729 --> 00:42:14,130
Ha. Here's the kicker, Jack.

466
00:42:14,298 --> 00:42:16,130
You didn't have to kill Arlene.

467
00:42:16,300 --> 00:42:19,668
Your wife's having an
affair with your chauffeur.

468
00:42:27,445 --> 00:42:28,674
Give it up, Jack.

469
00:43:32,210 --> 00:43:36,409
Six, seven, eight,
nine, 11 thousand.

470
00:43:36,581 --> 00:43:38,501
You know, Oscar, it
wouldn't have cost you a dime

471
00:43:38,649 --> 00:43:40,550
if the cops hadn't grabbed
that hundred grand.

472
00:43:40,718 --> 00:43:42,914
Well, what can I say?
You saved my life.

473
00:43:43,087 --> 00:43:45,056
Well, you saved mine.

474
00:43:45,223 --> 00:43:47,351
Here's your 10.
Tell Tony thanks.

475
00:43:47,525 --> 00:43:49,084
Yeah.

476
00:43:50,561 --> 00:43:54,623
- There's a game tonight. You coming?
- Yeah, maybe.

477
00:43:56,033 --> 00:43:59,993
Ah, Max, if you
ever need anything...

478
00:44:00,171 --> 00:44:01,901
- I'll let you know.
- Good luck to you.

479
00:44:02,073 --> 00:44:04,008
Good luck to you, Oscar.

480
00:44:12,517 --> 00:44:14,179
Oh.

481
00:44:16,387 --> 00:44:17,946
Phew.

482
00:44:19,357 --> 00:44:22,521
Ah, Jessie. Here are the rules.

483
00:44:22,693 --> 00:44:24,321
I like my life the way it is.

484
00:44:24,495 --> 00:44:26,123
I like the Lakers,
I like the track,

485
00:44:26,297 --> 00:44:28,664
I like Alison, and a
couple of other ladies.

486
00:44:28,833 --> 00:44:31,598
- Max.
- As for you, you behave yourself,

487
00:44:31,769 --> 00:44:34,102
you go to school and
you stay out of my cases,

488
00:44:34,272 --> 00:44:35,501
- you won't get bounced.
- Max.

489
00:44:35,673 --> 00:44:37,835
- What?
- I'm leaving.

490
00:44:38,376 --> 00:44:39,400
Where are you going?

491
00:44:40,578 --> 00:44:44,481
Alison found me a place and
I've got a line on a part-time job.

492
00:44:44,649 --> 00:44:46,914
I can't stay here, Max.
It just wouldn't work.

493
00:44:47,084 --> 00:44:51,078
We have too much
history, maybe not enough.

494
00:44:51,889 --> 00:44:53,414
You sure you wanna do this?

495
00:44:54,992 --> 00:44:56,893
I think I better.

496
00:45:00,231 --> 00:45:02,097
It's been swell. I'll call you.

497
00:45:02,266 --> 00:45:03,734
Wait.

498
00:45:05,169 --> 00:45:06,398
- Here.
- Max.

499
00:45:06,571 --> 00:45:09,006
It's your end of the job.

500
00:45:14,912 --> 00:45:16,380
Thank you.

501
00:45:45,910 --> 00:45:46,934
Hi, Mrs. Sanders.

502
00:45:47,111 --> 00:45:51,105
I'm sorry, my dear, but I've
decided not to rent the room after all.

503
00:46:10,468 --> 00:46:11,766
You try to provide for them,

504
00:46:11,936 --> 00:46:13,871
but no, they wanna
go off on their own

505
00:46:14,038 --> 00:46:16,098
and do God knows what
with god knows who...

506
00:46:16,274 --> 00:46:18,834
I should have known.

507
00:46:19,810 --> 00:46:22,143
Excuse me. Jessie, wait.

508
00:46:22,313 --> 00:46:24,513
What did you tell her, I was
a drug addict or something?

509
00:46:24,649 --> 00:46:26,169
I told her I wanted
you to stay with me

510
00:46:26,317 --> 00:46:28,684
so I could make
some things up to you.

511
00:46:28,853 --> 00:46:30,344
And she believed
that fairy tale?

512
00:46:30,921 --> 00:46:33,390
Some people know the
truth when they hear it.

513
00:46:43,134 --> 00:46:45,069
Let's go home.

514
00:46:47,438 --> 00:46:51,899
You know, Max, I think that we
actually work pretty well together.

515
00:46:52,076 --> 00:46:53,544
Yeah.

516
00:46:55,246 --> 00:46:56,270
Drive.

517
00:46:56,447 --> 00:46:58,712
Okay, Max, here are my rules.

518
00:46:58,883 --> 00:47:01,512
You don't tell me what to do.
- Unless it's necessary.

519
00:47:01,686 --> 00:47:03,606
You don't tell me I
sound like my mother.

520
00:47:03,754 --> 00:47:04,778
Unless you do.

521
00:47:04,955 --> 00:47:06,685
And I don't clean
the refrigerator.

522
00:47:06,857 --> 00:47:09,952
Well, that's all
right. Neither do I.

